  "description": "Production of potassium carbonate (potash) from wood ashes, mineral deposits, or brine evaporation. Potash is a fundamental alkali for glassmaking (potash glass), soap production, fertilizer, and chemical synthesis. Pearl ash (purified potash) was historically the primary source of alkali before synthetic soda ash.",
